In the preceding example, v16a is a virtual interface variable and its interface typespec
PBus is obtained by applying the npiTypespec one-to-one method.
The v16_phy variable is a virtual interface variable and its interface typespec Pbus.phy is
obtained by applying the npiTypespec one-to-one method.
The npiIsModport property of this interface typespec is 1 and itsnpiDefName is phy.
In addition, applying the npiParent one-to-one method to this typespec obtains the parent
interface typespec PBus.

* The npiDefName of an interface typespec that represents a modport that is the mod
port identifier.
The npiDefName of an interface typespec that represents an interface is the identifier
of the interface declaration.
* For an interface typespec that represents a modport, npiParent returns an interface
typespec of the corresponding interface.
For an interface typespec that represents an interface, npiParent returns NULL.
* In the following example, the first typedef defines an interface typespec corresponding
to virtual SBus(16) whose vpiName is SB16.
The npiDefName of this typespec is SBus, and the assigned parameter value of 16
is derived by iterating on npiParamAssign. The typedef SBphy, however, is an array
typespec for which the npiElemTypespec returns an interface typespec corresponding
to virtual SBus(32).phy.
The npiTypedef iteration from the module top returns handles to both SB16 and
SBphy interface typespecs.

