After scope manipulation, now hierarchy is:
"System/TOP/i_CPU/i_CCU/i_MODE"

Use npiUSN in Tcl Programming
The following example demonstrates how to manipulate SystemVerilog and VHDL scopes
using npiUSN.
construct a npiUSN handle for a string : "System.TOP.i_CPU.i_ALUB"
set hier_name "System.TOP.i_CPU.i_ALUB"
set delimiter "."
set usn_hdl [npi_usn_construct -fullname $hier_name -delimiter
$delimiter]
iterate every scopes and print to stdout
puts "== Dump the scope information =="
set scope_num [npi_usn_number -handle $usn_hdl]
for {set i 0} {$i<$scope_num} {incr i} {
puts "Scope($i) = \"[npi_usn_scope_name_at -handle $usn_hdl -position
$i]\""
}
remove the last scope
npi_usn_pop_back -handle $usn_hdl
"System.TOP.i_CPU"

; Hierarchy becomes:

get the last scope
set last_scope [npi_usn_back -handle $usn_hdl]
puts "Last scope = $last_scope" ; last_scope = i_CPU
add the last scope "i_CCU.i_MODE"
npi_usn_push_back -handle $usn_hdl -scope "i_CCU" ; Hierarchy becomes:
"System.TOP.i_CPU.i_CCU"
npi_usn_push_back -handle $usn_hdl -scope "i_MODE" ; Hierarchy becomes:
"System.TOP.i_CPU.i_CCU.i_MODE"
get the middle scope i_CPU.i_CCU : from scope 2 to scope 3
set middle_name [npi_usn_middle_name -handle $usn_hdl -from 2 -to 3]
puts "Middle name = \"$middle_name\"" ; Middle name: "i_CPU.i_CCU"

