The following is the coverage obtained from the simulation for the module test, which is

In the same report, you can also see the portion of the code that could not be covered
by the testbench, and therefore become targets or goals for the UNR analysis:
32 0/1 ==> ds <= 1'b1;
33 0/1 ==> state <= READ;
39 0/1 ==> DONE : state <= IDLE;
The VCS UNR flow looks for block level coverage and creates one coverage item (or
goal) per block.
In this example, lines 32 and 33 fall under the same “if block” as highlighted. As a
consequence, if line 32 (ds <= 1’b1) is covered, line 33 (state <= READ) also gets
covered:
DLY : if (!ws) begin
ds <= 1'b1;
state <= READ;
Therefore, UNR creates one goal for lines 32 and 33 and an additional goal for line 39.
This means that there are two uncovered goals for VCS UNR to check.

