Monitoring Toggle Coverage for an Array of Structures
VCS supports monitoring toggle coverage for arrays of
Toggle coverageSystemVerilog constructs
SystemVerilog structures. For each
structure in an array, toggle coverage is reported for each of the signal members of the
structure.
To monitor toggle coverage for an array of structures, no additional switch is required with
the -cm tgl compile-time option.
Example 2 illustrates the design that describes the toggle coverage of an array of packed
structures.
Example 2 Array of Packed Structures
'timescale 1ns/1ps
module myxmr();

typedef struct packed{
reg c;
reg f;
}t;

t [1:0]a[6:5];

myxmr xmr();
#10 xmr.a[5][0].c = 0;
#10 xmr.a[5][0].c = 1;
#10 xmr.a[6][1].f = 0;
#10 xmr.a[6][1].f = 1;
end

endmodule // test
