In this case, URG reports on only the branch starting and ending at r1. There is no new
branch starting at r3 because the if statement for r2 is excluded from coverage by the
//VCS coverage off pragma.

You can also use pragmas (see Example 39) to exclude code that does not affect branch
coverage, that is, the branches that VCS identify as unchanged. For example:
Example 39 Using Pragmas Without Affecting Branch Coverage
