The set_covergroup_expression syntax is supported under the -covg_enable_sce
switch at compile time, as follows:
vcs -covg_enable_sce
1) If the number of bins specified is more than the size of the array given on the
right side, the number of bins is reduced to the size of the array.
2) If the array given on the right side is dynamic array or queue, it might be
empty. If it is empty, then the bin being defined on the left side is discarded.
3) If the set_covergroup_expression syntax is used in the code and the
-covg_enable_sce switch is not used at compile time, VCS gives an error
message. An example of the error message is as follows:
Error-[FC-SCE] Set Covergroup Expressions not supported in
default
test5.v, 16
m, "bins b1 = arr;"
Currently support for set covergroup expressions is available
under VCS compile time switch
