fullexclude.fsm file includes all the excludable objects of FSM coverage – states
and transitions. To exclude any specific state, transition of a FSM or the whole FSM
from the FSM coverage report, uncomment the corresponding exclusion entries in the
fullexclude.fsm file.
Example 55 is the design used to describe the FSM metric.
Example 55 Design Used to Describe the FSM Metric
1 module top;
2 reg x, y, z;
4 fsm1 fsmOne();
5 fsm2 fsmTwo();

