The assert_no_underflow checker continuously monitors the test_expr at every positive
edge of the triggering event or clock clk. This assertion verifies that test_expr never:
• Changes value from a min value (default = 0) to a value less than min,
or
• Changes to a value greater than or equal to max (default (2**width)-1).
The test_expr can be any valid Verilog expression.
assert_no_underflow [#( severity_level, width, min, max,
min
Minimum value sampled at clock (t) of clk with default value of 0.
max
Maximum value sampled at clock (t+1) of clk with default value of (2**width - 1 ).

