Verifying the Memory Controller
To completely check the functionality of the memory controller, you have to perform a
series of tests. First, verify the controller’s reset by writing a task. Then, write tasks to
check the read and write operations of the controller. Also check the integrity of the read
and write operations. Finally, check the address map (all 256 addresses) exhaustively for
the read and write functions.
This section focuses on checking the memory controller by emulating both the system bus
and the memory bus behavior. Rather than connecting the RTL models of the memory to
the controller, model the behavior of the four different memory devices in the testbench.
