wire n;
electrical n;
Improved Partitioning Format for Sharing Hierarchical Information
The final parameter values for boundary Spice primitives and sub-circuits are passed via a
partition file in hierarchical format. The structure of this partition file has been optimized to
enhance simulation performance.
To enable this feature, use the -adopt sp_param_part_enh compile option. If necessary,
you can disable this optimization using the -adopt no_snps_param_hva_file_enh
compile option.
Inherited-Connection-Based Supply Specification for
Verilog-AMS Designs
In Verilog-AMS flow the interfaces between analog and digital blocks are realized by the
automatic insertion of connect modules. To configure a connect module instance, you
need the ability to associate the proper supply information with it. Other than connect
modules, you may also need to pass the supply information through the design hierarchy
where the components may not have supply (power, ground) ports.
These functionalities can be supported through inherited connection where the supply
information is specified through the analog front-end tool. You may provide supply
information at the upper level of the design, and then this information propagates
transitively downwards through the design hierarchy. A lower level block inherits this
supply information that is coming from its upper layer, unless another supply specification
that targets a lower-level component, overrides this data.
This feature supports supply routing via Verilog-AMS netlist through inherited connection
and associates this supply with the connect module instances and the SPICE or Verilog-
AMS blocks those that need this information for simulation purposes.
Connect-Definition Commands
The analog front-end provides all the connect-def commands to VCS through the analog-
control (vcsAD.init) file.
You can use these connect-definition commands to specify the inherited connection-based
supply information for a Verilog-AMS design.

connectmodule D2A (l, e);
input l; logical l;
output e; electrical e;
analog begin
V(e) <+ (l == 1'b1) ? 3.3 : 0.0;
end

connectrules mixedsignal;
connect D2A merged input logical, output electrical;
endconnectrules
