Considerations for Export DPI_SC Tasks
Considerations for Export DPI_SC Tasks
Export DPI_SC is used for calling time-consuming Verilog tasks from SystemC.
The export DPI_SC function has same signature as regular export DPI function but it
requires two extra arguments in the end.
This function must always be called from SC_THREAD or SC_CTHREAD.
SV has a time consuming task blocking_SV_task(). To call it from SC_THREAD, export
it as DPI_SC as follows:
SystemVerilog File: top.v
module TOP;
scmodel sc_i();
initial #100 $finish;
task blocking_SV_task(input int n);
$display("vlog %0d ns: blocking_SV_task(%0d) starts", $time, n);
#1 $display("vlog %0d ns: blocking_SV_task(%0d) still busy", $time, n);
#1 $display("vlog %0d ns: blocking_SV_task(%0d) ends", $time, n);
endtask // block_SV_task
export "DPI_SC" task blocking_SV_task;
import "DPI" context task init_register_sv_scope();
initial init_register_sv_scope();
endmodule;
