Example 10 SystemC Code With sc_vector
SC_MODULE(mod)
{
sc_in<bool> reset_n_i;
sc_vector<sc_in<double> > rx1_data_I_i; //sc_vector ports declared
sc_vector<sc_out<double> > rx1_data_O_i; //sc_vector ports declared
myVHDL vh1; //VHDL instance
SC_CTOR(mod) :
reset_n_i("reset_n_i")
, rx1_data_I_i("rx1_data_I_i", 16) //16 ports created
, rx1_data_O_i("rx1_data_O_i", 16) //16 ports created
{
for(i=0;i<16;i++)
{
vh1.rx1_data_I_i[i].bind(rx1_data_I_i[i]); //16 Port connected
vh1.rx1_data_O_i[i].bind(rx1_data_O_i[i]); //16 Port Connected
}
}
Specify the -sc_portmap option to parse the portmap file, as shown in the following
command line:
% vhdlan -sc_model myVHDL myVHDL.vhdl -sc_portmap myVHDL.map
The portmap file identifies the ports that are to be bundled into the sc_vector construct.
For information about creating and using the portmap file, see section Using the Port Map
File. The following is a sample portmap file:
## myVHDL.map
## portname bits hdl-type sysc-type isvector OSCI-
name
reset_n_i 1 bit bool
rx1_data_I_i_* 64 real double sc_vector
rx1_data_I_i
rx1_data_O_i_* 64 real double sc_vector
rx1_data_O_i

